## Docker
{% if choices.docker == "full" %}
Everything runs in containers. The `dev` service mounts this folder and keeps the virtual environment in a Docker volume:

```sh
docker compose run --rm dev uv sync                # after cloning or changing dependencies
docker compose up dev                              # playground + polling, restarting on changes
docker compose run --rm dev uv run poe check       # any task
docker compose up --build app                      # production container, /health on http://localhost:{{ ports.APP_PORT }}/health
docker compose build app                           # only build the production image
docker compose --profile dev down                  # stop everything; add -v to also delete the volumes
```
{% else %}
```sh
docker compose up --build   # build the image and run the bot; /health on http://localhost:{{ ports.APP_PORT }}/health
docker compose logs -f      # follow the logs
docker compose down         # stop; add -v to also delete the database volume
docker compose build app    # only build the production image
```
{% endif %}
The image (`python:3.14-slim`) contains the locked production dependencies and `app/`, runs `python -m app run` as a non-root user and restarts unless stopped. Compose passes `.env` to the container. The SQLite database is stored {% if choices.data == "local" %}in the project's `data/` folder (`DOCKER_DATA=./data`){% else %}in the Docker volume `data` (`DOCKER_DATA=data`){% endif %}; change `DOCKER_DATA` in `.env` to switch.
{% endif %}
